must not disclose it to anyone else until the licensor has fixed it or 90 days
have passed since your report. You may test the software for flaws in good
faith on copies you run under section 2, and the licensor will bring no claim
against you for that testing. Good faith means testing only to find and fix
flaws, in a way designed to avoid harm, and using what you learn mainly to
improve security. These terms authorise no access to any service, account or
data; the service terms govern that.

